--- released-v1/docs/coop/design-corrections/native/native-capability-matrix.v2.json
+++ current-v2/docs/coop/design-corrections/native/native-capability-matrix.v2.json
@@ -164,9 +164,16 @@
    "standing": "The `authenticated release declaration registry` named by native-evidence section 1.4 and admission-and-qualification section 1.1. Its CONTENT is release-specific and remains an authenticated INPUT - which rows a given release ships is not a contract constant - but its SCHEMA, its membership authority, its canonical spelling and its binding to the Plan are normative and are stated here.",
    "schema": "native/native-evidence.schemas.v2.json#/$defs/ReleaseCapabilityRegistryV1",
    "row": "{capabilityId, languageModes[]}",
-   "membershipAuthority": "capabilityId MUST be a member of this document's capabilities[].id, and every entry of languageModes MUST be a member of this document's languageModes with a cell that is not NOT-SELECTED. A row spelled preview-* is refused, as it already was. The registry may declare a SUBSET of the matrix - a release need not ship everything - but never a member the matrix does not register.",
-   "bindingToPlan": "default_capability_selection emits one analysis-spec row per (registry row, unit whose languageMode the row applies to), required=true, provenance=DEFAULTED, in canonical-set order, with a duplicate refusing rather than silently deduping. The emitted capabilityId is the registry row's, which is the matrix id, so the DEFAULT and EXPLICIT paths agree on one vocabulary by construction.",
-   "notASubstituteForAdmission": "The default helper is one producer of an analysis-spec, not the authority. The same vocabulary is closed again where it matters - at Plan/Run closure over the RETAINED analysis-spec - so an explicitly configured or hand-built spec is judged by the same rule as a defaulted one."
+   "membershipAuthority": "capabilityId MUST be a member of this document's capabilities[].id, and every entry of languageModes MUST be a member of this document's languageModes with a cell that is not NOT-SELECTED. A row spelled preview-* is refused, as it already was. A row may never name a member the matrix does not register.",
+   "bindingToPlan": "default_capability_selection emits one analysis-spec row per (unit, capability REQUIRED BY THE MATRIX for that unit's languageMode) - see requiredDefault - with required=true, provenance=DEFAULTED, in canonical-set order, and a duplicate refuses rather than silently deduping. The emitted capabilityId is the matrix id, so the DEFAULT and EXPLICIT paths agree on one vocabulary by construction. An earlier revision of THIS sentence said one row per (registry row, unit), which was the release-driven recipe requiredDefault replaces; two normative recipes cannot both stand, and this is the one.",
+   "notASubstituteForAdmission": "The default helper is one producer of an analysis-spec, not the authority. The same vocabulary is closed again where it matters - at Plan/Run closure over the RETAINED analysis-spec - so an explicitly configured or hand-built spec is judged by the same rule as a defaulted one.",
+   "itIsAvailabilityNotScope": "NORMATIVE, and the correction of an earlier sentence that read `the registry may declare a SUBSET of the matrix - a release need not ship everything`. That sentence was written about MEMBERSHIP and read as permission about SCOPE. The registry states which capabilities THIS BUILD SHIPS. It never states which capabilities the product SELECTS: that is fixed by this matrix, and admission section 1.1 and native section 1.4 both require the `default` profile to be the complete intended product. Driving the default FROM the registry let a staged build shipping three rows silently request three capabilities and still look conformant, which is the D-371 selected product quietly shrinking with nothing disclosed anywhere.",
+   "requiredDefault": "For each discovered unit the `default` profile MUST request EVERY capability whose (capability, unit languageMode) cell is not NOT-SELECTED - that is the published definition of the selected product, since NOT-SELECTED means `outside D-371; no promise`. UNSUPPORTED-TYPED cells are INCLUDED deliberately: the matrix says such a cell `refuses with the named deficiency; never silently narrows`, and the way it never silently narrows is that the default asks and the Run answers with the disclosed unavailable pair. Omitting it would leave a consumer with no record that the capability exists and was not served.",
+   "absenceIsDisclosedNotDropped": "A capability the selected product requires and this release does not declare available is still REQUESTED, and the selection boundary records the absence in default_capability_selection's `undeclaredCapabilities`. That record is an AVAILABILITY ACCOUNT, not a CoverageResultV3 and not a final (deficiency, nativeCause) pair - see absenceProjectionAndPrecedence. No new vocabulary, no new public code, and no preview or default exception.",
+   "installedAvailabilityVersusQualification": "Declaring availability is NOT qualification and cannot promote a cell. platformQualified stays false, no cell is QUALIFIED here, and SUPPORTED-DESIGN remains `contracted behavior, corpus named, qualification pending` whatever a release declares. A staged or development build that ships fewer providers is an availability fact disclosed per request; it is not a narrowed product, not a completed release qualification, and not a licence to restate the matrix.",
+   "explicitOverride": "Explicit user configuration - product-configuration analysis.capabilities, same vocabulary - overrides the REQUEST, not this obligation. An override is a recorded choice carrying its own provenance (the default's is DEFAULTED); it is a user narrowing their own analysis, which is visible, and never a host silently narrowing the product, which would not be.",
+   "hostInputBoundary": "Stated honestly: WHICH rows a release ships is an authenticated input this contract cannot measure, and nothing here qualifies a build, an installer or a provider. What is contract is the obligation the default must meet, the vocabulary and membership the declaration is held to, and the disclosure an absence owes.",
+   "absenceProjectionAndPrecedence": "What an absence PROJECTS to depends on the capability, and neither case may be assumed. (1) PRECEDENCE. A capability can be undeclared AND unservable by the admitted universe at the same time - references under syntax-only is both. The syntax capability prerequisite DERIVES language-tier-unsupported / capability-missing for such a scope and refuses anything else, and the section 10 precedence ranks language-tier-unsupported ahead of provider-unavailable, so the more specific one wins and the release-absence account never overrides it. The final Coverage pair remains the owning derivation's. Where no more specific deficiency applies, provider-unavailable with capability-missing is the applicable pair, routed by section 10 to the existing COVERAGE.PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE. (2) CANDIDATE-ONLY CAPABILITIES. clones-near and clones-cross-tsjs have EMPTY `relations` here: they are candidate-only by section 6.1 authority, mint no fact and no relation@rung, and therefore have NO Coverage entry that could carry a pair. Requiring an owed Coverage for them would mean fabricating a relation. Their absence account is the selection record itself, projection `selection-account-only`; fact-producing capabilities carry projection `coverage-entry` and name the exact relation@rung coordinates they project onto. An availability account may be shared by all capabilities; it is not automatically a CoverageResultV3 for any of them."
   },
   "enforcedAt": "native_evidence_model admit_requested_capabilities (the analysis-spec boundary) and admit_release_capability_registry (the authenticated input boundary), and again at foundation close_run over the retained analysis-spec, beside the languageMode join that was already there.",
   "unchanged": "No capability is added, removed or renamed; no cell state changes; the six advertised language modes, the native contexts and the full default-selected product all stay exactly as representable as before. This publishes the authority for a field that had none."
